package cajeta.nucleo.expr;

/**
 * Fused tensor expressions (nucleo-expr spec §2, §3, §5): the `Fuse`
 * transform intrinsic and its `@Fuse` annotation sugar.
 *
 * `Fuse` is a COMPILER INTRINSIC, not a method of this class: applied to a
 * statically-known elementwise tensor expression, it collapses N tensor
 * operators into ONE loop over the element index at compile time — no
 * expression-graph object at runtime, no per-operator temporaries, only the
 * result tensor is allocated. This file is the importable home of the
 * contract, beside the transform combinators ([[Transforms]]).
 *
 * - `Fuse(f)` for `f : (Tensor<E>) -> Tensor<E>` yields a REUSABLE compiled
 *   function with f's signature whose body is one fused pass. Building it
 *   runs nothing; the CALL is the force point (there is no `.eval`).
 * - A reduction (`Tensor.sum` / `mean` / `std`) bounds the fusion region: it
 *   stages as its own pass, and the elementwise tail after it fuses — the
 *   standardize shape `(t - mean(t)) / std(t)` runs as its reduction stages
 *   plus one fused loop. A reduction as the WHOLE expression fuses the
 *   elementwise body INTO its accumulation (`Fuse(t -> sum(t*t))` is
 *   scalar-valued and allocates nothing).
 * - A shared sub-expression is computed once (the DAG dedups leaves), and a
 *   staged reduction is hoisted once.
 * - `@Fuse` on a static single-return method fuses its body through the SAME
 *   recognizer — sugar only, identical results and identical allocations.
 *
 * THE AUTOGRAD SEAM (spec §8): `Fuse` and `Grad` are two consumers of the
 * same forward DAG. `Grad(Fuse(f))` — or the `@Grad @Fuse` stack —
 * differentiates the fused expression: the gradient is identical to the
 * unfused form's, the backward is ordinary IR (`Jit` fuses it like any other
 * function), and an expression that is never differentiated carries no
 * autograd machinery at all.
 *
 * A body that cannot fuse — an op outside the elementwise set (`matmul`), or
 * `std` as the whole expression — is the named, located compile error
 * CAJETA_ERROR_TRANSFORM_NOT_FUSIBLE, never a silent eager fallback.
 */
public final class Expr {
    private Expr() { }
}
